  "presentation_summary": [
    "12-year-old girl admitted for jaundice and dark urine.",
    "She was subfebrile with otherwise normal vital signs.",
    "Exam showed jaundice; no rash, diarrhea, vomiting, arthralgia, dysuria, exudative pharyngotonsillitis, or cervical lymphadenopathy; mild hepatosplenomegaly was reported.",
    "Initial labs showed hemoglobin 8.7 g/dL, WBC 17.9 x10^9/L with lymphocyte predominance, platelets 180 x10^9/L, total bilirubin 7.08 mg/dL, indirect bilirubin 5.23 mg/dL, AST 122 U/L, ALT 101 U/L, LDH 1303 U/L, and haptoglobin 7 mg/dL.",
    "By the next day, hemoglobin dropped to 6.3 g/dL and reticulocytes were 4.57%; smear showed anisocytosis.",
    "DAT for cold agglutinins was positive for C3 3+ and EBV VCA IgM/IgG were positive; these confirmatory and etiology facts are retained with use_in_ranking:false."
